{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29990 - PROTEIN:6154",
  "verbalization": "Isotorachrysone appears to have a mechanistic link to Prelamin-A/C through a series of target interactions. The drug is identified as a target of Ataxin-2 and Diplotrin A, both of which are themselves targets of Prelamin-A/C. This suggests a potential pathway where Isotorachrysone influences the activity of Ataxin-2, which in turn modulates Diplotrin A, which ultimately affects Prelamin-A/C. The shared involvement of Diplotrin A in multiple pathways reinforces the possibility of a functional relationship between Isotorachrysone and Prelamin-A/C. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the regulation of protein targets, though the exact nature of the interaction between Isotorachrysone and Ataxin-2 remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Isotorachrysone to exert a biological effect on Prelamin-A/C through a cascade of molecular interactions.",
